  "source_review": [
    "REQALLENTS hook bracket encloses only the existing exact send_command call after successful GROUPS ownership/release. UDP instance maps to actual link; committed Tx assignment supplies actual private packet ID, never next-ID reservation or arbitrary send order.",
    "Pump snapshots selected Tx ID and prior sent flag before actual callback; a send-begin hook opens one bounded in-flight observation. Exact callback return is captured before original failure return. This fixes the synchronous UDP io_failure close/clear gap found in the first E review.",
    "First retirement reason latches before generic clear. While a matching callback is in flight, identity keys survive synchronous close/clear; its post-callback failure is counted, then keys clear. Witness storage is separate from cleared Tx storage; original send/ACK/timeout results are unchanged.",
    "Peer ACK observation occurs only in original used+sent+matching-ID removal branch after frame decoding. ACK precedes further application payload validation and is transport-only; unsent/wrong/corrupt ACKs and arbitrary queue disappearance do not establish application receipt.",
    "All protocol hooks return void and only mutate the optional separate witness. Wrapper refusal/absence still delegates original service/close/cancel/timeout once with unchanged arguments/result. TLS scope unwinds at each normal wrapper exit, including refused observations; no callback controls queueing, send, retry, ACK, deadline or close.",
    "Witness is capped at 256 bytes, one caller thread only; capture/link keys are borrowed identities, not owned objects. Caller must forbid concurrent/reentrant witness access and retire before capture destruction; active destroy deliberately refuses to free. Output span cannot overlap witness; private pointers/IDs/payloads/credentials/generations never appear in diagnostic struct.",
    "Protocol-return status range is full existing CohStatus 0..7; deferred COH_NOT_FOUND is distinct from hard callback failures, and invalid status refuses the observer. Public counters/offsets have explicit caps. All server/source/character/actor/application-ACK/world authority flags remain zero."
  ],
